      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This review summarizes recent developments in the context of the neurochemical classification of nociceptors and explores the relationships between functionally and neurochemically defined subgroups. Although the complete picture is not yet available, several lines of intriguing evidence suggest that despite the complexity and diversity of nociceptor properties, a relatively \"simple\" neurochemical classification fits well with several recently identified molecular characteristics."},
